# VITE_API_BASE_URL: Base URL of the RiskSearcher backend API (FastAPI/persistent server).
# Set this in your local environment or deployment platform. Do not commit a
# production backend URL to source control.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=""

# Add any client-safe public keys here (e.g. WalletConnect Project ID, Circle publishable key).
# Never put server-side secrets (LLM API keys, Circle secret keys) in a VITE_-prefixed var —
# anything prefixed VITE_ is bundled into client-side JS and publicly readable.

# World ID — public App ID from developer.world.org (safe client-side).
VITE_WORLD_APP_ID=""

# World ID — WORLD_ID_RP_ID and WORLD_ID_RP_SIGNING_KEY are read directly by
# interface/api/world-id-rp-signature.ts (a Vercel serverless function, not
# the browser bundle) via process.env — set them as plain project env vars
# in the Vercel dashboard, NOT here and NOT VITE_-prefixed. The signing_key
# especially must never end up client-visible.
